      "math_academy_id": "e-4974",
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(-2,0)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x)$. Find a point that must lie on $y=f(x-7).$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x-7)$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $7$ units to the *right*. So the $y$-coordinate remains unchanged while the $x$-coordinate increases by $7.$\n\nWe know that the point $(-2,0)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(-2+7,0) = (5,0)$ must lie on $y=f(x-7).$",
